patch_description:
None of the three prompt styles worked on explanatory tasks. "Fast forum regular", "plain one-person voice" and "newspaper register" all scored 88-95 on Pangram. The failing texts read as careful, well-edited explanations, and that seems to be what triggers the detector. The only texts that passed were rewrites of human reviews. Those have strong personal reactions, a quirky voice, colloquial asides and imperfect polish. The target examples show the same traits: "Um, I'm having oral surgery here, lady", "I guess...", rhetorical questions, and wry judgments.

This edit swaps the register to a casual Reddit or texting style. It allows:

- lowercase starts, "tbh", "iirc", "lol", "kinda", "pretty much";
- minor grammatical looseness and run-ons;
- opinionated reactions and asides to the reader;
- admitted uncertainty ("from what I remember").

It still forbids invented facts and anecdotes, keeps the answer correct and on-task, and keeps the length target. Rewrites stay faithful to the source. Thinking stays short, and temperature drops slightly to 0.9 to keep coherence.
